  "summary": "PASS: The Heart That Learns to Love was read continuously as adult-parish speech and compared with the expansive study's healed-charity argument and the complete concise study; its concrete opening, both Gospel movements, Pauline charity, petitions for healing, Eucharistic hope and practicable response form a coherent, speakable argument without invented experience, clerical identity, unsupported attribution, a composed prayer or dependence on scholarly apparatus. Exact checks covered the 1962 Missal images at pp. 398\u2013400, retained Douay\u2013Rheims Matthew 22:34\u201346/Ephesians 4:1\u20136/Psalm 118:124,137, Augustine De doctrina I.22.20\u201321 and Psalm 118 English paragraph 123, Chrysostom Matthew homily 71, the Dessain Super Ephesios 4 lecture 1 images at pp. 312\u2013315, and retained Summa III.79.1\u20132,6 corpus and 6 ad 1; all eight sealed files remain unchanged, the separate note accurately records 1,283 spoken words and a 10.7\u201311.7-minute estimate at 110\u2013120 words per minute, and this written/source review claims neither timed human delivery nor final visual acceptance."
